{"author":{"id":"7be502fc1252faa17034e20337c97f83224cb75681f6f2358da33e4e8d7e55b6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794790064,"nonce":"+L7jSzXQzP1Pyb0MdFYPVQyhz5Q=","title":"Static file server does not receive request headers: no 304 / no Accept-Encoding handling","message":"Hello Zentinel team,\n\nthank you for Zentinel. While serving a small static site with a `static-files` route we noticed that conditional requests and compression negotiation have no effect. This is a low-priority observation.\n\nObserved (tag 26.11_2, commit ea8ccf0):\n\n- A request with If-None-Match set to the ETag from a previous response returns 200 with the full body instead of 304.\n- A request with Accept-Encoding: br, gzip returns an uncompressed body, without a Content-Encoding header.\n\nCause as far as we can tell: handle_static_route (crates/proxy/src/proxy/handlers.rs:43-54) builds a new http::Request for the static file server from the method and URI only (handlers.rs:46-50). The request headers are not copied. The static file server reads If-None-Match (crates/proxy/src/static_files/mod.rs:280 and 404) and Accept-Encoding (negotiate_encoding, called at mod.rs:294-298) from that request, so these code paths cannot see the client headers when called through the proxy.\n\nSuggestion: pass the original request headers (at least If-None-Match, If-Modified-Since, Range, Accept-Encoding) on to the static file server.\n\nNote: compression only applies from 1 KB (MIN_COMPRESS_SIZE, mod.rs:44), which is fine; this report is about the headers not arriving.\n\nHappy to test a fix. Thank you.","files":null}]}